     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. The total daily dose looks unusually high, so I want to check it with you first.\n\n**The problem:** 1700 mg three times daily comes to **5100 mg/day**. The usual maximum for immediate-release metformin is **2550 mg/day**, and for extended-release it's **2000 mg/day**. This order is about twice the IR maximum. Higher doses don't control blood sugar much better but do raise the risk of stomach side effects and lactic acidosis.\n\n**What you may have meant:**\n- **850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals** (2550 mg/day, the IR maximum). 850 mg is a standard tablet size, and 1700 mg is twice that, so this seems the most likely intent.\n- **1700 mg by mouth twice daily with meals** (3400 mg/day). This is still above the labeled maximum, so it would need confirmation too.\n- **1000 mg by mouth twice daily** (2000 mg/day), a common maintenance dose.\n\nPlease tell me which dose you want. If you really did mean 1700 mg three times daily, confirm that and give a brief reason, and I'll enter it with your reason in the order note so pharmacy can see it when they verify."
      }
     ],
